	(text "ISP2454 notes (datasheet R7):\n- Antenna, 32 MHz + 32.768 kHz crystals, DC-DC inductor and all decoupling are inside. No external parts.\n- OUT_ANT (20) must be joined to OUT_MOD (22) by a short trace (net ANT_LINK).\n- Pads 49-62 are mechanical: isolated copper in the footprint, not in this symbol.\n- Antenna corner 1 mm from the board edge, no copper or parts on any layer in the keep-out,\n  including the folded battery layer below it.\n- Firmware: set LFXO load capacitance to 19 pF (devicetree load-capacitance-femtofarad = <19000>).\n- Every signal uses an OUTER-row pad, so the flex needs no via-in-pad. Inner GND pads (21, 23) and\n  nRESET (13) may use tented vias under the module centre, as the datasheet allows.\n- I2C on TWIM30 (P0, low-power domain). UART on UARTE20 (P1).\n- P1.02/P1.03 are NFC pins: left unused. P2 trace pins left unused.\n- GPIO plan and reasons: docs/flex-rev-a-pinout.md"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 20.32 0)
